-- haa-alif
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"atoll_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","atoll_sections":[{"heading":"Welcome to Haa Alifu Atoll","paragraphs":["Haa Alifu Atoll, the northernmost atoll in the Maldives, offers a unique blend of rich cultural heritage and untouched natural beauty. Also known as Thiladhunmathi Uthuruburi, this atoll is closer to India than to the Maldivian capital Male, giving it a distinctive character and traditions.","With its pristine white sand beaches, vibrant coral reefs, and authentic Maldivian island life, Haa Alifu provides visitors with an off-the-beaten-path experience. The atoll is particularly known for its traditional lacquer work, unique dialect, and important historical sites dating back to the pre-Islamic period."]},{"heading":"Exceptional Dive Sites in Haa Alifu","paragraphs":["Seasonal cleaning station where majestic manta rays gather from August to November, offering incredible encounters.","Depth: 12-25m | Level: Intermediate | Season: Aug-Nov","Thrilling drift dive through a channel frequented by gray reef sharks, white tip reef sharks, and occasional hammerheads.","Depth: 15-40m | Level: Advanced | Current: Strong"]},{"heading":"Cultural & Adventure Activities","paragraphs":["Visit traditional islands to see lacquerware artisans, local crafts, and experience authentic Maldivian hospitality.","Explore vibrant coral gardens and encounter tropical fish, turtles, and reef sharks in crystal-clear waters.","Experience authentic Maldivian night fishing techniques followed by a beach barbecue of your catch."]},{"heading":"Traveling to Haa Alifu Atoll","paragraphs":["Haa Alifu Atoll is accessible via domestic flight from Velana International Airport (MLE):","Most resorts arrange combined flight+speedboat transfers for guests."]},{"heading":"Haa Alifu Atoll Island Highlights","paragraphs":["Haa Alifu''s Pristine Islands"]},{"heading":"Best Time to Visit Haa Alifu Atoll","paragraphs":["The ideal time to visit Haa Alifu Atoll depends on your interests:"]},{"heading":"Visitor Experiences","paragraphs":["Haa Alifu was the highlight of our Maldives trip! The cultural tours to local islands gave us insight into authentic Maldivian life that you don''t get in the more touristy atolls. The diving was spectacular too - we saw mantas at Manta Point and had incredible shark encounters at Shark Channel.","The remoteness of Haa Alifu makes it special. Our resort felt like our own private paradise. The traditional lacquerware demonstration on Utheemu Island was fascinating. Only giving 4 stars because the domestic flight transfer was a bit long after our international flight."]}]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'haa-alif';

-- haa-dhaalu
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"atoll_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","atoll_sections":[{"heading":"Welcome to Haa Dhaalu Atoll","paragraphs":["Haa Dhaalu Atoll, the southern part of the Thiladhunmathi Atoll, offers visitors an authentic Maldivian experience with its unspoiled natural beauty and rich cultural traditions. As one of the northernmost atolls, Haa Dhaalu remains less developed than southern atolls, preserving its traditional way of life.","The atoll is renowned for its spectacular coral reefs, abundant marine life, and some of the Maldives'' most beautiful uninhabited islands. The capital island Kulhudhuffushi is known for its vibrant culture and traditional crafts, particularly its lacquer work and woven palm leaf products."]},{"heading":"Exceptional Dive Sites in Haa Dhaalu","paragraphs":["Seasonal cleaning station where majestic manta rays gather from August to November, offering incredible encounters.","Depth: 12-25m | Level: Intermediate | Season: Aug-Nov","Thrilling drift dive through a channel frequented by gray reef sharks, white tip reef sharks, and occasional hammerheads.","Depth: 15-40m | Level: Advanced | Current: Strong"]},{"heading":"Cultural & Adventure Activities","paragraphs":["Visit traditional islands to see lacquerware artisans, local crafts, and experience authentic Maldivian hospitality.","Explore vibrant coral gardens and encounter tropical fish, turtles, and reef sharks in crystal-clear waters.","Experience authentic Maldivian night fishing techniques followed by a beach barbecue of your catch."]},{"heading":"Traveling to Haa Dhaalu Atoll","paragraphs":["Haa Dhaalu Atoll is accessible via domestic flight from Velana International Airport (MLE):","Most resorts arrange combined flight+speedboat transfers for guests."]},{"heading":"Haa Dhaalu Atoll Island Highlights","paragraphs":["Haa Dhaalu''s Pristine Islands"]},{"heading":"Best Time to Visit Haa Dhaalu Atoll","paragraphs":["The ideal time to visit Haa Dhaalu Atoll depends on your interests:"]},{"heading":"Visitor Experiences","paragraphs":["Haa Dhaalu was the perfect escape from the busier tourist areas. The cultural tours to local islands were incredibly authentic, and the diving was world-class. We saw mantas, sharks, and even a whale shark during our stay. The Northern Paradise Resort was exceptional with its eco-friendly approach.","The remoteness of Haa Dhaalu makes it special. Our resort felt like our own private paradise. The traditional lacquerware demonstration on Nellaidhoo Island was fascinating. Only giving 4 stars because the domestic flight transfer was a bit long after our international flight."]}]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'haa-dhaalu';

-- shaviyani
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"atoll_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","atoll_sections":[{"heading":"Welcome to Shaviyani Atoll","paragraphs":["Shaviyani Atoll (also known as North Miladhunmadulu) is a pristine paradise located in the far northern part of the Maldives archipelago, approximately 160 km north of Male''. This remote atoll offers visitors an authentic Maldivian experience away from the more developed tourist areas, with untouched natural beauty and traditional island culture.","Known for its spectacular marine life, pristine coral reefs, and emerging luxury resorts, Shaviyani Atoll represents the Maldives as it once was - unspoiled, tranquil, and breathtakingly beautiful. The atoll''s remote location has preserved its natural environment and traditional way of life, providing a glimpse into authentic Maldivian culture.","With its mix of exclusive luxury resorts, traditional local islands, and spectacular underwater landscapes, Shaviyani Atoll provides an idyllic escape for travelers seeking both relaxation and adventure in one of the Maldives'' most untouched settings."]},{"heading":"Unique Features of Shaviyani Atoll","paragraphs":["Shaviyani Atoll is home to several manta ray cleaning stations where these majestic creatures gather to have parasites removed by smaller fish. These sites offer divers and snorkelers the rare opportunity to observe manta rays up close in their natural habitat, particularly during the northeast monsoon season.","The atoll features some of the most untouched coral reefs in the Maldives, with vibrant marine life and excellent visibility. Less visited than the central atolls, Shaviyani''s reefs have suffered minimal tourism impact and offer spectacular diving and snorkeling experiences with healthy coral formations.","Shaviyani Atoll is renowned for its traditional boat building craftsmanship. Several islands in the atoll maintain the ancient art of constructing dhonis (traditional Maldivian boats) using techniques passed down through generations, offering visitors a glimpse into this important aspect of Maldivian maritime heritage."]},{"heading":"World-Class Diving in Shaviyani Atoll","paragraphs":["Shaviyani Atoll is renowned for its exceptional diving conditions, with pristine reefs, diverse marine life, and excellent visibility. The atoll''s remote location means many dive sites are virtually untouched, offering exclusive underwater experiences for diving enthusiasts.","A famous cleaning station where manta rays gather to have parasites removed by cleaner wrasse. This site offers divers the incredible opportunity to observe these majestic creatures up close as they hover above coral bommies, particularly during the northeast monsoon season from December to April.","Depth: 10-25m | Best Conditions: Northeast monsoon (Dec-Apr)","A stunning underwater pinnacle featuring dramatic overhangs and swim-throughs covered in colorful soft corals. The site attracts a variety of pelagic species including grey reef sharks, eagle rays, and large schools of jackfish and barracuda, especially when currents are strong.","Depth: 15-40m | Best Conditions: Year-round, best visibility Dec-Apr","A unique dive site featuring the world''s first semi-submerged art installation created by British artist Jason deCaires Taylor. This underwater sculpture gallery also serves as an artificial reef, attracting a variety of marine life and providing an otherworldly diving experience that combines art and nature.","Depth: 3-12m | Best Conditions: Year-round","A beautiful reef system featuring extensive hard coral formations and abundant reef fish. The site is known for its resident population of reef sharks, turtles, and occasional manta ray sightings. The shallow reef top makes it ideal for both diving and snorkeling.","Depth: 5-25m | Best Conditions: Year-round"]},{"heading":"Popular Activities in Shaviyani Atoll","paragraphs":["Explore the vibrant house reefs surrounding the islands of Shaviyani Atoll, home to an incredible diversity of marine life including reef sharks, rays, turtles, and colorful reef fish. The clear waters and healthy coral formations make for exceptional snorkeling experiences.","Visit traditional Maldivian islands to experience authentic local culture, including boat building workshops, traditional crafts, cuisine, and daily island life. These tours provide insights into the rich cultural heritage of the Maldives beyond the luxury resort experience.","Shaviyani Atoll is home to several species of dolphins, including spinner dolphins and bottlenose dolphins. Take a boat trip to witness these playful creatures in their natural habitat, often performing acrobatic jumps and spins, especially during sunset cruises."]},{"heading":"More Things to Do in Shaviyani Atoll","paragraphs":["Swim with gentle giants of the oceanDuration: 2hrs","Traditional line fishing at sunsetDuration: 2hrs","Explore the underwater art installationDuration: 2hrs","Experience authentic Maldivian lifeDuration: 4hrs","Private lunch on pristine sandbankDuration: 3hrs","Learn traditional dhoni craftsmanshipDuration: 3hrs"]},{"heading":"Getting to Shaviyani Atoll","paragraphs":["Shaviyani Atoll is located approximately 160 km north of Male'' and can be reached by:","For guests staying at Fairmont Sirru Fen Fushi, the resort arranges combined seaplane transfers from Male'' International Airport. Those staying on local islands can arrange transfers through their guesthouses or use public transportation options."]},{"heading":"Shaviyani Atoll Transfers","paragraphs":["Male'' to Fairmont Sirru Fen Fushi","Male'' to Shaviyani Atoll"]},{"heading":"Best Time to Visit Shaviyani Atoll","paragraphs":["The best time to visit Shaviyani Atoll depends on your preferences:","For the ultimate Shaviyani Atoll experience, visit between December and April when the weather is at its best and underwater visibility is exceptional for diving and snorkeling. This period also coincides with manta ray season, offering the best chance to encounter these magnificent creatures."]},{"heading":"Discover Shaviyani Atoll Islands","paragraphs":["Shaviyani Atoll has a rich cultural heritage that dates back centuries. The atoll''s inhabited islands preserve traditional Maldivian customs, architecture, and way of life that have remained largely unchanged for generations.","Key cultural highlights include:","Visitors to Shaviyani Atoll have the unique opportunity to experience authentic Maldivian culture by visiting local islands and interacting with communities that maintain their traditional way of life.","The islands of Shaviyani Atoll maintain strong cultural traditions that are still practiced in daily life. Visitors can witness traditional music and dance performances (Boduberu), observe skilled craftsmen at work, and participate in local festivities during religious and cultural celebrations.","Several guesthouses and resorts in the atoll offer cultural excursions to local islands, providing insights into traditional Maldivian life beyond the luxury resort experience. These tours often include visits to local homes, schools, and workshops where traditional crafts are practiced."]},{"heading":"Cultural Heritage of Shaviyani Atoll","paragraphs":["Shaviyani Atoll has a rich cultural heritage that dates back centuries. The atoll''s inhabited islands preserve traditional Maldivian customs, architecture, and way of life that have remained largely unchanged for generations.","Key cultural highlights include:","Visitors to Shaviyani Atoll have the unique opportunity to experience authentic Maldivian culture by visiting local islands and interacting with communities that maintain their traditional way of life.","The islands of Shaviyani Atoll maintain strong cultural traditions that are still practiced in daily life. Visitors can witness traditional music and dance performances (Boduberu), observe skilled craftsmen at work, and participate in local festivities during religious and cultural celebrations.","Several guesthouses and resorts in the atoll offer cultural excursions to local islands, providing insights into traditional Maldivian life beyond the luxury resort experience. These tours often include visits to local homes, schools, and workshops where traditional crafts are practiced."]}]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'shaviyani';

-- noonu
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"atoll_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","atoll_sections":[{"heading":"Welcome to Noonu Atoll","paragraphs":["Noonu Atoll, located in the northern part of the Maldives approximately 180 km north of Male'', is renowned for its pristine natural beauty, crystal-clear waters, and some of the most exclusive luxury resorts in the world. This stunning atoll offers visitors an unparalleled Maldivian experience with its untouched coral reefs, abundant marine life, and secluded islands.","Known for hosting ultra-luxury resorts like Soneva Jani and Velaa Private Island, Noonu Atoll has become synonymous with high-end tourism and exceptional service. The atoll''s relative seclusion from the more developed central atolls has preserved its natural environment, making it a paradise for nature lovers and those seeking privacy and exclusivity.","With its perfect blend of luxury accommodations, spectacular underwater landscapes, and authentic Maldivian culture on local islands, Noonu Atoll provides an idyllic escape for travelers seeking the ultimate Maldivian experience in one of the country''s most pristine settings."]},{"heading":"Unique Features of Noonu Atoll","paragraphs":["Noonu Atoll is home to some of the most iconic and photographed overwater villas in the world, particularly the water villas with slides at Soneva Jani. These architectural marvels have become symbols of Maldivian luxury and feature innovative designs that blend seamlessly with the natural environment.","The atoll boasts some of the most pristine and untouched marine environments in the Maldives. Its relative distance from the more developed central atolls has preserved its coral reefs and marine ecosystems, offering exceptional diving and snorkeling experiences with vibrant coral formations and abundant marine life.","Noonu Atoll''s northern location and minimal light pollution create perfect conditions for stargazing. Several resorts in the atoll, particularly Soneva Jani with its dedicated observatory, offer exceptional stargazing experiences where guests can observe celestial bodies through powerful telescopes under the guidance of resident astronomers."]},{"heading":"World-Class Diving in Noonu Atoll","paragraphs":["Noonu Atoll is renowned for its exceptional diving conditions, with pristine reefs, diverse marine life, and excellent visibility. The atoll''s relative seclusion means many dive sites are virtually untouched, offering exclusive underwater experiences for diving enthusiasts.","A stunning dive site named after its distinctive Christmas tree-shaped rock formation. The site features vibrant coral gardens, overhangs, and swim-throughs where divers can spot reef sharks, eagle rays, and large schools of snappers and fusiliers.","Depth: 10-30m | Best Conditions: Year-round, best visibility during northeast monsoon (Dec-Apr)","A thrilling channel dive known for its strong currents and pelagic encounters. This underwater pinnacle attracts grey reef sharks, eagle rays, and occasionally manta rays during the northeast monsoon. The vibrant soft corals and overhangs add to the site''s appeal.","Depth: 15-40m | Best Conditions: Northeast monsoon (Dec-Apr)","A beautiful reef corner featuring extensive hard coral formations and abundant reef fish. The site is ideal for underwater photography and relaxed exploration with excellent visibility and minimal currents, making it perfect for beginners and snorkelers.","Depth: 5-20m | Best Conditions: Year-round","A stunning channel dive where the outer reef meets the deep blue, creating a perfect environment for marine life. Divers can expect to see napoleon wrasse, turtles, reef sharks, and occasionally manta rays during the northeast monsoon season.","Depth: 10-30m | Best Conditions: Northeast monsoon (Dec-Apr)"]},{"heading":"Popular Activities in Noonu Atoll","paragraphs":["Explore the vibrant house reefs surrounding the islands of Noonu Atoll, home to an incredible diversity of marine life including reef sharks, rays, turtles, and colorful reef fish. The clear waters and healthy coral formations make for exceptional snorkeling experiences.","Take advantage of Noonu Atoll''s minimal light pollution to observe the night sky in all its glory. Several resorts offer dedicated stargazing experiences with professional telescopes and resident astronomers who guide guests through the wonders of the cosmos.","Visit traditional Maldivian islands to experience authentic local culture, including fishing demonstrations, traditional crafts, cuisine, and daily island life. These tours provide insights into the rich cultural heritage of the Maldives beyond the luxury resort experience."]},{"heading":"More Things to Do in Noonu Atoll","paragraphs":["Watch playful dolphins at sunsetDuration: 2hrs","Relaxing treatments beneath the oceanDuration: 2hrs","Movies under the starsDuration: 3hrs","Private lunch on pristine sandbankDuration: 3hrs","Guided stargazing with astronomerDuration: 2hrs","Learn to prepare traditional Maldivian dishesDuration: 3hrs"]},{"heading":"Getting to Noonu Atoll","paragraphs":["Noonu Atoll is located approximately 180 km north of Male'' and can be reached by:","For guests staying at luxury resorts, the properties typically arrange transfers from Male'' International Airport. Maafaru International Airport in Noonu Atoll now also accepts private jets, making the atoll more accessible for VIP travelers."]},{"heading":"Noonu Atoll Transfers","paragraphs":["Male'' to Noonu Atoll Resorts","Male'' to Noonu Atoll via Maafaru"]},{"heading":"Best Time to Visit Noonu Atoll","paragraphs":["The best time to visit Noonu Atoll depends on your preferences:","For the ultimate Noonu Atoll experience, visit between December and April when the weather is at its best and underwater visibility is exceptional for diving and snorkeling. However, the luxury resorts in Noonu Atoll offer exceptional experiences year-round, with indoor activities and spa treatments available during occasional rain showers."]},{"heading":"Discover Noonu Atoll Islands","paragraphs":["Noonu Atoll has a rich cultural heritage that reflects traditional Maldivian island life. Despite the development of luxury tourism in the region, many local islands maintain their traditional practices and customs.","Key cultural highlights include:","Visitors to Noonu Atoll have the opportunity to experience authentic Maldivian culture through visits to local islands, where traditional ways of life continue alongside the development of luxury tourism in the region.","The islands of Noonu Atoll maintain strong cultural traditions that are still practiced in daily life. Visitors can witness traditional music and dance performances (Boduberu), observe skilled craftsmen at work, and participate in local festivities during religious and cultural celebrations.","Several resorts in the atoll have developed cultural exchange programs that allow guests to visit local islands and interact with communities, providing authentic insights into traditional Maldivian island life while supporting local economies."]},{"heading":"Cultural Heritage of Noonu Atoll","paragraphs":["Noonu Atoll has a rich cultural heritage that reflects traditional Maldivian island life. Despite the development of luxury tourism in the region, many local islands maintain their traditional practices and customs.","Key cultural highlights include:","Visitors to Noonu Atoll have the opportunity to experience authentic Maldivian culture through visits to local islands, where traditional ways of life continue alongside the development of luxury tourism in the region.","The islands of Noonu Atoll maintain strong cultural traditions that are still practiced in daily life. Visitors can witness traditional music and dance performances (Boduberu), observe skilled craftsmen at work, and participate in local festivities during religious and cultural celebrations.","Several resorts in the atoll have developed cultural exchange programs that allow guests to visit local islands and interact with communities, providing authentic insights into traditional Maldivian island life while supporting local economies."]}]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'noonu';

-- raa
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"atoll_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","atoll_sections":[{"heading":"Welcome to Raa Atoll","paragraphs":["Raa Atoll (also known as North Maalhosmadulu) is a pristine paradise located in the northern part of the Maldives archipelago, approximately 142 km north of Male''. This stunning atoll offers visitors a perfect blend of luxury, adventure, and authentic Maldivian experiences away from the more crowded central atolls.","Known for its untouched natural beauty, vibrant coral reefs, and growing collection of luxury resorts, Raa Atoll has emerged as one of the Maldives'' most sought-after destinations. The atoll''s remote location has preserved its pristine environment and traditional island culture, providing a more authentic Maldivian experience.","With its mix of world-class luxury resorts, traditional local islands, and spectacular marine life, Raa Atoll provides an idyllic escape for travelers seeking both relaxation and adventure in one of the Maldives'' most beautiful settings."]},{"heading":"Unique Features of Raa Atoll","paragraphs":["Raa Atoll is home to some of the Maldives'' most spectacular bioluminescent beaches, where the shoreline glows with blue light at night due to marine plankton. This magical natural phenomenon creates an otherworldly experience for visitors, particularly on Vaadhoo Island, known as the \"Sea of Stars.\"","The atoll features some of the most well-preserved coral reefs in the Maldives, with vibrant marine life and excellent visibility. Less visited than the central atolls, Raa''s reefs have suffered less from tourism impact and offer spectacular diving and snorkeling experiences with healthy coral formations.","Raa Atoll''s inhabited islands maintain strong traditional Maldivian culture and way of life. Visitors can experience authentic island communities, traditional crafts like boat building and lacquer work, and local cuisine that has remained largely unchanged for generations."]},{"heading":"World-Class Diving in Raa Atoll","paragraphs":["Raa Atoll is renowned for its exceptional diving conditions, with pristine reefs, diverse marine life, and excellent visibility. The atoll''s remote location means many dive sites are less frequented, offering more exclusive underwater experiences.","A thrilling drift dive along a dramatic wall drop-off with overhangs and caves. The site is known for its strong currents that attract pelagic species including grey reef sharks, eagle rays, and large schools of jacks and barracuda.","Depth: 15-30m | Best Conditions: Northeast monsoon (Dec-Apr)","A fascinating maze of coral formations creating swim-throughs and channels. This site offers a unique topography with abundant marine life including reef sharks, turtles, and a variety of colorful reef fish. The coral gardens are particularly impressive.","Depth: 10-25m | Best Conditions: Year-round","A submerged pinnacle rising from the deep ocean floor, known for its vibrant soft corals and marine biodiversity. Divers regularly encounter schools of snappers, groupers, and occasional manta rays during the northeast monsoon season.","Depth: 18-40m | Best Conditions: December-April","A shallow reef system perfect for beginners and snorkelers, featuring extensive hard coral formations and abundant reef fish. The site is ideal for underwater photography and relaxed exploration of the atoll''s marine ecosystem.","Depth: 5-15m | Best Conditions: Year-round"]},{"heading":"Popular Activities in Raa Atoll","paragraphs":["Explore the vibrant house reefs surrounding the islands of Raa Atoll, home to an incredible diversity of marine life including reef sharks, rays, turtles, and colorful reef fish. The clear waters and healthy coral formations make for exceptional snorkeling experiences.","Experience the magical phenomenon of bioluminescent plankton lighting up the shoreline at night, creating a natural light show that resembles a sea of stars. Vaadhoo Island is particularly famous for this natural wonder, best viewed during new moon periods.","Visit traditional Maldivian islands to experience authentic local culture, including traditional crafts, cuisine, and daily island life. These tours provide insights into the rich cultural heritage of the Maldives beyond the luxury resort experience."]},{"heading":"More Things to Do in Raa Atoll","paragraphs":["Encounter playful dolphins in their natural habitatDuration: 2hrs","Traditional line fishing at sunsetDuration: 2hrs","Witness the magical sea of starsDuration: 2hrs","Experience authentic Maldivian lifeDuration: 4hrs","Private lunch on pristine sandbankDuration: 3hrs","Rejuvenating treatments in paradiseDuration: 2-3hrs"]},{"heading":"Getting to Raa Atoll","paragraphs":["Raa Atoll is located approximately 142 km north of Male'' and can be reached by:","For guests staying at luxury resorts, the properties typically arrange combined transfers from Male'' International Airport. Those staying on local islands can arrange transfers through their guesthouses or use public transportation options."]},{"heading":"Raa Atoll Transfers","paragraphs":["Male'' to Raa Atoll Resorts","Male'' to Raa Atoll"]},{"heading":"Best Time to Visit Raa Atoll","paragraphs":["The best time to visit Raa Atoll depends on your preferences:","For the ultimate Raa Atoll experience, visit between December and April when the weather is at its best and underwater visibility is exceptional for diving and snorkeling. However, if you want to experience the bioluminescent beaches at their most spectacular, plan your visit during the southwest monsoon season."]},{"heading":"Discover Raa Atoll Islands","paragraphs":["Raa Atoll has a rich cultural heritage that dates back centuries. The atoll''s inhabited islands preserve traditional Maldivian customs, architecture, and way of life that have remained largely unchanged for generations.","Key cultural highlights include:","Visitors to Raa Atoll have the unique opportunity to experience authentic Maldivian culture by visiting local islands and interacting with communities that maintain their traditional way of life.","The islands of Raa Atoll maintain strong cultural traditions that are still practiced in daily life. Visitors can witness traditional music and dance performances (Boduberu), observe skilled craftsmen at work, and participate in local festivities during religious and cultural celebrations.","Several guesthouses and resorts in the atoll offer cultural excursions to local islands, providing insights into traditional Maldivian life beyond the luxury resort experience. These tours often include visits to local homes, schools, and workshops where traditional crafts are practiced."]},{"heading":"Cultural Heritage of Raa Atoll","paragraphs":["Raa Atoll has a rich cultural heritage that dates back centuries. The atoll''s inhabited islands preserve traditional Maldivian customs, architecture, and way of life that have remained largely unchanged for generations.","Key cultural highlights include:","Visitors to Raa Atoll have the unique opportunity to experience authentic Maldivian culture by visiting local islands and interacting with communities that maintain their traditional way of life.","The islands of Raa Atoll maintain strong cultural traditions that are still practiced in daily life. Visitors can witness traditional music and dance performances (Boduberu), observe skilled craftsmen at work, and participate in local festivities during religious and cultural celebrations.","Several guesthouses and resorts in the atoll offer cultural excursions to local islands, providing insights into traditional Maldivian life beyond the luxury resort experience. These tours often include visits to local homes, schools, and workshops where traditional crafts are practiced."]}]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'raa';

-- baa
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"atoll_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","atoll_sections":[{"heading":"Welcome to Baa Atoll","paragraphs":["Baa Atoll is one of the Maldives'' most celebrated destinations, designated as a UNESCO Biosphere Reserve in 2011 for its exceptional marine biodiversity. Located in the central western part of the Maldives, this atoll is home to Hanifaru Bay, one of the world''s largest manta ray feeding destinations.","With its pristine coral reefs, vibrant marine life, and commitment to sustainable tourism, Baa Atoll offers visitors a perfect blend of luxury and environmental consciousness. The atoll features some of the Maldives'' most exclusive eco-friendly resorts alongside traditional Maldivian island communities."]},{"heading":"Best Dive Sites in Baa Atoll","paragraphs":["World-famous marine protected area where hundreds of manta rays and whale sharks gather to feed on plankton between May and November.","Depth: 5-15m | Level: All levels | Best Time: May-November","Vibrant reef with stunning coral formations, home to reef sharks, eagle rays, and a diverse array of tropical fish species.","Depth: 10-30m | Level: Intermediate | Best Time: Year-round"]},{"heading":"Popular Activities in Baa Atoll","paragraphs":["Experience the thrill of swimming alongside gentle giants at Hanifaru Bay, one of the world''s largest manta ray feeding stations.","Visit traditional Maldivian islands like Eydhafushi and Thulhaadhoo to experience authentic culture and witness local craftsmanship.","Embark on a sunset cruise to spot playful spinner dolphins that frequently visit the waters around Baa Atoll."]},{"heading":"Baa Atoll Activities","paragraphs":["Swim with majestic manta rays at Hanifaru BayDuration: 3hrs","Explore local islands & traditional cultureDuration: 6 hrs","Sunset cruise with spinner dolphinsDuration: 2hrs","Private picnic on pristine sandbankDuration: 4hrs","Learn about traditional Maldivian craftsDuration: 5hrs","Traditional line fishing + BBQ dinnerDuration: 3hrs"]},{"heading":"Getting to Baa Atoll","paragraphs":["Baa Atoll is located approximately 126 km northwest of Male'' and can be reached by:","Most luxury resorts in Baa Atoll arrange seaplane transfers directly from Male'' International Airport."]},{"heading":"Baa Atoll Transfers","paragraphs":["Baa Atoll","Baa Atoll","Baa Atoll","Baa Atoll","Baa Atoll","Baa Atoll","Baa Atoll"]},{"heading":"Best Time to Visit Baa Atoll","paragraphs":["The best time to visit Baa Atoll depends on your interests:","For the ultimate Baa Atoll experience, visit between June and October when manta rays gather in large numbers at Hanifaru Bay."]},{"heading":"Discover Baa Atoll Islands","paragraphs":["In June 2011, Baa Atoll was designated as a UNESCO Biosphere Reserve, recognizing its exceptional biodiversity and the sustainable development practices implemented by local communities and resorts.","The reserve covers the entire atoll, including:","Visitors to Baa Atoll are encouraged to practice responsible tourism and follow guidelines to help preserve this unique ecosystem for future generations.","This protected marine area is world-famous for the spectacular natural phenomenon that occurs between May and November when hundreds of manta rays and whale sharks gather to feed on plankton.","Strict regulations are in place to protect this unique ecosystem, including limited visitor numbers and guided snorkeling only."]},{"heading":"UNESCO Biosphere Reserve","paragraphs":["In June 2011, Baa Atoll was designated as a UNESCO Biosphere Reserve, recognizing its exceptional biodiversity and the sustainable development practices implemented by local communities and resorts.","The reserve covers the entire atoll, including:","Visitors to Baa Atoll are encouraged to practice responsible tourism and follow guidelines to help preserve this unique ecosystem for future generations.","This protected marine area is world-famous for the spectacular natural phenomenon that occurs between May and November when hundreds of manta rays and whale sharks gather to feed on plankton.","Strict regulations are in place to protect this unique ecosystem, including limited visitor numbers and guided snorkeling only."]}]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'baa';

-- lhaviyani
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"atoll_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","atoll_sections":[{"heading":"Welcome to Lhaviyani Atoll","paragraphs":["Lhaviyani Atoll, also known as Faadhippolhu Atoll, is a stunning northern atoll in the Maldives known for its pristine beaches, crystal-clear waters, and exceptional diving spots. Located about 120km north of Male, this atoll offers a perfect blend of seclusion and accessibility.","With its vibrant coral reefs, abundant marine life, and luxurious resorts, Lhaviyani Atoll is a dream destination for divers, honeymooners, and luxury travelers. The atoll features some of the Maldives'' most exclusive resorts, each offering world-class amenities and breathtaking overwater villas."]},{"heading":"World-Class Dive Sites in Lhaviyani","paragraphs":["Famous drift dive site with strong currents that attract large pelagics including sharks, rays, and tuna.","Depth: 15-40m | Level: Advanced | Season: Year-round","Two sunken ships (Victoria and Fesdu) that have become artificial reefs teeming with marine life.","Depth: 12-30m | Level: Intermediate | Season: Year-round"]},{"heading":"Adventure & Relaxation Activities","paragraphs":["Explore vibrant coral reefs just steps from your resort with abundant marine life including turtles and reef sharks.","Try your luck at catching tuna, wahoo, and sailfish in the rich fishing grounds around Lhaviyani Atoll.","Glide across the calm lagoon waters while enjoying panoramic views of the atoll."]},{"heading":"Traveling to Lhaviyani Atoll","paragraphs":["Lhaviyani Atoll is accessible from Velana International Airport (MLE):","Most luxury resorts include seaplane transfers in their packages."]},{"heading":"Lhaviyani Atoll Island Highlights","paragraphs":["Lhaviyani''s Stunning Islands"]},{"heading":"Best Time to Visit Lhaviyani Atoll","paragraphs":["The ideal time to visit depends on your interests:"]},{"heading":"Visitor Experiences","paragraphs":["Our honeymoon at Komandoo Island Resort was absolutely perfect. The private beach dinners were magical, and the diving at Kuredu Express was exhilarating - we saw several reef sharks and a huge school of eagle rays. The staff went above and beyond to make our stay special.","The Shipyard wreck dive was the highlight of my trip - two massive wrecks covered in coral and teeming with fish. The resort (Kuredu) was excellent, though the house reef had some areas of coral bleaching. Overall an amazing diving destination."]}]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'lhaviyani';

-- kaafu
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"atoll_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","atoll_sections":[{"heading":"Welcome to Kaafu Atoll","paragraphs":["Kaafu Atoll, also known as Male'' Atoll, is the most visited atoll in the Maldives and home to the capital city Male''. This atoll is divided into North Male'' Atoll and South Male'' Atoll, offering some of the most accessible and luxurious resort experiences in the country.","With its proximity to Velana International Airport, Kaafu Atoll is often the first taste visitors get of the Maldives'' stunning beauty. The atoll features crystal-clear lagoons, vibrant coral reefs, and some of the most famous dive sites in the world."]},{"heading":"Best Dive Sites in Kaafu Atoll","paragraphs":["One of the first dive sites discovered in Maldives, famous for its dramatic overhangs and coral formations.","Depth: 5-30m | Level: All levels","Excellent drift dive site with strong currents attracting large pelagics like sharks and rays.","Depth: 15-30m | Level: Advanced"]},{"heading":"Popular Activities in Kaafu Atoll","paragraphs":["Explore vibrant coral gardens and marine life at house reefs of resorts or on snorkeling excursions.","Relaxing dhoni cruises at sunset, often with dolphin spotting opportunities.","Visit traditional fishing villages and experience authentic Maldivian culture."]},{"heading":"Kaafu Atoll Activities","paragraphs":["Organized By: Male Atoll ActivitiesLocation: Male Atoll","Explore with GoPro, towels & pickupDuration: 2hrs","Includes: GoPro, Softdrinks, PickupDuration: 3-5hrs","Explore local islands & sandbanksDuration: 4 hrs","Duration: 9hrs | Includes: Shipwreck, Nurse Shark, Sandbank","Duration: 3hrs | Equipment & Boat Included","Evening boat trip + BBQ your own catch","Duration: 7hrs | Includes Fishing & Lunch","Cultural trip with snorkeling & sandbank"]},{"heading":"Getting to Kaafu Atoll","paragraphs":["Kaafu Atoll resorts are the most accessible in Maldives, with transfer times ranging from:","Many resorts offer 24/7 speedboat transfers due to the proximity to the airport."]},{"heading":"Kaafu Atoll Transfers","paragraphs":["South Male Atoll","North Male Atoll","South Male Atoll","South Male Atoll","North Male Atoll","North Male Atoll","North Male Atoll","North Male Atoll","North Male Atoll","South Male Atoll","South Male Atoll","North Male Atoll","North Male Atoll","North Male Atoll","South Male Atoll","North Male Atoll","North Male Atoll","North Male Atoll","North Male Atoll","South Male Atoll","North Male Atoll","North Male Atoll","North Male Atoll","North Male Atoll","North Male Atoll","North Male Atoll","North Male Atoll","North Male Atoll","North Male Atoll","North Male Atoll","North Male Atoll","South Male Atoll","South Male Atoll","North Male Atoll","South Male Atoll","North Male Atoll","South Male Atoll","North Male Atoll","South Male Atoll","South Male Atoll","North Male Atoll"]},{"heading":"Best Time to Visit Kaafu Atoll","paragraphs":["The best time to visit Kaafu Atoll is during the dry season from November to April when you can expect calm seas, plenty of sunshine, and excellent visibility for diving and snorkeling.","The surf season runs from March to October, with the biggest swells typically in June-August."]},{"heading":"Discover Kaafu Atoll Islands","paragraphs":["Kaafu Atoll was absolutely breathtaking! The resorts were luxurious and the diving at Banana Reef was unforgettable. We saw so many colorful fish and even a turtle!"]}]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'kaafu';

-- alif-alif
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"atoll_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","atoll_sections":[{"heading":"Welcome to Alifu Alifu Atoll","paragraphs":["Alifu Alifu Atoll, also known as Ari Atoll, is one of the most popular atolls in the Maldives, renowned for its spectacular diving spots, luxury resorts, and breathtaking natural beauty. Located west of Male, this atoll offers the perfect blend of accessibility and tropical paradise.","With its crystal-clear waters, vibrant coral reefs, and abundant marine life including whale sharks and manta rays, Alifu Alifu is a dream destination for divers and snorkelers. The atoll features some of the Maldives'' most exclusive resorts, each offering world-class amenities and stunning overwater villas."]},{"heading":"World-Class Dive Sites in Alifu Alifu","paragraphs":["Famous cleaning station where majestic manta rays gather year-round, with peak season from May to November.","Depth: 5-20m | Level: Beginner-Intermediate | Season: Year-round (peak May-Nov)","One of the best places in the world to swim with gentle whale sharks, most commonly seen from August to November.","Depth: 5-30m | Level: All levels | Season: Year-round (peak Aug-Nov)"]},{"heading":"Adventure & Relaxation Activities","paragraphs":["Swim with the ocean''s gentle giants on guided snorkeling excursions to whale shark hotspots.","Evening boat trips to spot playful spinner dolphins against breathtaking Maldivian sunsets.","Pamper yourself with luxurious treatments in overwater spa pavilions with ocean views."]},{"heading":"Traveling to Alifu Alifu Atoll","paragraphs":["Alifu Alifu Atoll is easily accessible from Velana International Airport (MLE):","Most luxury resorts include seaplane transfers in their packages."]},{"heading":"Alifu Alifu Atoll Island Highlights","paragraphs":["Alifu Alifu''s Stunning Islands"]},{"heading":"Best Time to Visit Alifu Alifu Atoll","paragraphs":["The ideal time to visit depends on your interests:"]},{"heading":"Visitor Experiences","paragraphs":["Our stay at Conrad Maldives in Alifu Alifu was beyond magical. Swimming with whale sharks was the highlight of our trip - an experience we''ll never forget. The underwater restaurant was worth every penny, with incredible food and marine life views. Can''t wait to return!","Alifu Alifu''s diving is world-class. We did 12 dives and saw mantas every time at Manta Point. The house reef at Veligandu Island Resort was teeming with life. Only reason for 4 stars was some coral bleaching we noticed, but the marine life was still abundant."]}]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'alif-alif';

-- alif-dhaalu
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"atoll_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","atoll_sections":[{"heading":"Welcome to Alifu Dhaalu Atoll","paragraphs":["Alifu Dhaalu Atoll, the southern part of Ari Atoll, is a diver''s paradise renowned for its spectacular marine life and luxurious resorts. This central atoll offers some of the best opportunities in the Maldives to encounter whale sharks, manta rays, and vibrant coral reefs.","With its convenient location just west of Male, Alifu Dhaalu combines easy accessibility with pristine natural beauty. The atoll features a mix of exclusive resort islands and traditional fishing villages, offering visitors both luxury and cultural experiences."]},{"heading":"Exceptional Dive Sites in Alifu Dhaalu","paragraphs":["One of the most reliable spots in the Maldives to encounter gentle whale sharks year-round.","Depth: 5-30m | Level: All levels | Season: Year-round","Cleaning station where majestic manta rays gather, especially from May to November.","Depth: 10-20m | Level: Beginner-Intermediate"]},{"heading":"Adventure & Relaxation Activities","paragraphs":["Swim alongside these gentle giants in their natural habitat with expert guides.","Evening boat trips to spot playful spinner dolphins against breathtaking sunsets.","Pamper yourself with luxurious treatments in overwater spa pavilions."]},{"heading":"Traveling to Alifu Dhaalu Atoll","paragraphs":["Alifu Dhaalu Atoll is easily accessible from Velana International Airport (MLE):","Most luxury resorts include seaplane transfers in their packages."]},{"heading":"Best Time to Visit Alifu Dhaalu Atoll","paragraphs":["The ideal time to visit depends on your interests:"]},{"heading":"Visitor Experiences","paragraphs":["Our stay at Mirihi Island Resort was absolute perfection! The house reef was incredible - we saw turtles, reef sharks, and countless colorful fish right from our villa. The whale shark snorkeling excursion was the highlight of our trip. The crew knew exactly where to find these gentle giants!","Alifu Dhaalu''s diving is world-class. We did 10 dives and saw mantas at Manta Point on every dive! The visibility was excellent and marine life abundant. Constance Moofushi was luxurious but we wish there were more dining options. Would still highly recommend for divers!"]}]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'alif-dhaalu';

-- vaavu
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"atoll_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","atoll_sections":[{"heading":"Discover Vaavu Atoll","paragraphs":["Vaavu Atoll, officially known as Felidhu Atoll, stands as one of the most unspoiled and naturally beautiful atolls in the Maldives archipelago. Comprising 19 islands (only 5 inhabited), this atoll offers visitors an authentic Maldivian experience with its pristine beaches, vibrant coral reefs, and traditional island life.","Renowned among divers worldwide, Vaavu Atoll boasts some of the most spectacular dive sites in the Maldives, including the legendary Fotteyo Kandu channel and the famous Alimatha Jetty night dive where nurse sharks and stingrays gather in large numbers."]},{"heading":"World-Class Diving in Vaavu Atoll","paragraphs":["Widely regarded as the best channel dive in Maldives, featuring dramatic overhangs, caves, and abundant pelagic life including gray reef sharks, eagle rays, and large schools of fish.","Depth: 10-40m | Level: Advanced | Current: Strong","Iconic night dive where dozens of nurse sharks and stingrays gather to feed under the jetty lights, offering one of the most unique diving experiences in the Maldives.","Depth: 5-15m | Level: All levels | Visibility: Excellent"]},{"heading":"Unforgettable Experiences in Vaavu Atoll","paragraphs":["Visit traditional Maldivian fishing villages and uninhabited islands to experience authentic local culture and pristine beaches.","Explore vibrant coral gardens and encounter tropical fish, turtles, and reef sharks in crystal-clear waters.","Witness playful spinner dolphins at sunset while enjoying breathtaking views of the Maldivian horizon."]},{"heading":"Traveling to Vaavu Atoll","paragraphs":["Vaavu Atoll is conveniently accessible from Velana International Airport (MLE) via:","Most resorts arrange private transfers, while guesthouses typically use scheduled speedboat services.","Vaavu Atoll''s Pristine Islands"]},{"heading":"Vaavu Atoll Island Highlights","paragraphs":["Vaavu Atoll''s Pristine Islands"]},{"heading":"Ideal Time to Experience Vaavu Atoll","paragraphs":["The optimal time to visit Vaavu Atoll is during the dry northeast monsoon season from December to April, when conditions are perfect for diving and water activities:","For underwater photographers, January-March offers the clearest waters and best marine life encounters."]},{"heading":"Explore Vaavu Atoll''s Islands","paragraphs":["Vaavu Atoll exceeded all our expectations! The diving at Fotteyo Kandu was absolutely breathtaking - we saw multiple gray reef sharks, a school of eagle rays, and the healthiest coral formations we''ve ever encountered. Our resort (Alimatha Aquatic) was perfect for divers with its house reef and excellent dive center.","The night dive at Alimatha Jetty was the highlight of our Maldives trip - swimming with dozens of nurse sharks and stingrays under the lights was an unforgettable experience. Vaavu offers a more authentic Maldivian experience compared to the more developed atolls."]},{"heading":"Visitor Experiences","paragraphs":["Vaavu Atoll exceeded all our expectations! The diving at Fotteyo Kandu was absolutely breathtaking - we saw multiple gray reef sharks, a school of eagle rays, and the healthiest coral formations we''ve ever encountered. Our resort (Alimatha Aquatic) was perfect for divers with its house reef and excellent dive center.","The night dive at Alimatha Jetty was the highlight of our Maldives trip - swimming with dozens of nurse sharks and stingrays under the lights was an unforgettable experience. Vaavu offers a more authentic Maldivian experience compared to the more developed atolls."]}]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'vaavu';

-- meemu
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"atoll_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","atoll_sections":[{"heading":"Welcome to Meemu Atoll","paragraphs":["Meemu Atoll, officially known as Mulaku Atoll, is a pristine paradise located in the central part of the Maldives archipelago, approximately 120 km south of Male''. This relatively untouched atoll offers visitors an authentic Maldivian experience with its pristine natural beauty, vibrant marine life, and traditional island culture.","Known for its spectacular diving sites, untouched coral reefs, and exclusive luxury resorts, Meemu Atoll represents the Maldives in its most natural and serene state. The atoll''s relative seclusion has preserved both its natural environment and traditional way of life, providing a glimpse into authentic Maldivian culture away from the more developed tourist areas.","With its perfect blend of luxury resorts, traditional local islands, and spectacular underwater landscapes, Meemu Atoll provides an idyllic escape for travelers seeking both relaxation and adventure in one of the Maldives'' most pristine settings."]},{"heading":"Unique Features of Meemu Atoll","paragraphs":["Meemu Atoll is home to some of the most untouched and vibrant coral reefs in the Maldives. Less visited than the central atolls, Meemu''s reefs have suffered minimal tourism impact and offer spectacular diving and snorkeling experiences with healthy coral formations and abundant marine life.","The atoll is renowned for its exceptional shark encounters, particularly with reef sharks and occasionally whale sharks. The channels between islands create perfect conditions for these magnificent creatures, offering divers and snorkelers the opportunity to observe them in their natural habitat.","Meemu Atoll maintains a strong traditional fishing heritage, with many locals still practicing sustainable fishing methods passed down through generations. Visitors can observe and even participate in traditional fishing techniques, offering a glimpse into this important aspect of Maldivian maritime culture."]},{"heading":"World-Class Diving in Meemu Atoll","paragraphs":["Meemu Atoll is renowned for its exceptional diving conditions, with pristine reefs, diverse marine life, and excellent visibility. The atoll''s relative seclusion means many dive sites are virtually untouched, offering exclusive underwater experiences for diving enthusiasts.","A thrilling channel dive known for its strong currents and pelagic encounters. The site features dramatic drop-offs where divers can spot grey reef sharks, eagle rays, and large schools of jacks and barracuda, especially when currents are strong.","Depth: 15-40m | Best Conditions: Year-round, best visibility during northeast monsoon (Dec-Apr)","A popular dive site known for its abundant reef shark population. This channel dive offers excellent opportunities to observe grey reef sharks, white tip reef sharks, and occasionally hammerhead sharks. The vibrant soft corals and overhangs add to the site''s appeal.","Depth: 10-30m | Best Conditions: Year-round","A beautiful underwater pinnacle featuring extensive hard coral formations and abundant reef fish. The site is ideal for underwater photography and relaxed exploration of the atoll''s marine ecosystem with excellent visibility and minimal currents.","Depth: 5-20m | Best Conditions: Year-round","A stunning reef corner where the outer reef meets the channel, creating a perfect environment for marine life. Divers can expect to see napoleon wrasse, turtles, reef sharks, and occasionally manta rays during the northeast monsoon season.","Depth: 10-25m | Best Conditions: Northeast monsoon (Dec-Apr)"]},{"heading":"Popular Activities in Meemu Atoll","paragraphs":["Explore the vibrant house reefs surrounding the islands of Meemu Atoll, home to an incredible diversity of marine life including reef sharks, rays, turtles, and colorful reef fish. The clear waters and healthy coral formations make for exceptional snorkeling experiences.","Visit traditional Maldivian islands to experience authentic local culture, including fishing demonstrations, traditional crafts, cuisine, and daily island life. These tours provide insights into the rich cultural heritage of the Maldives beyond the luxury resort experience.","Experience the traditional Maldivian way of fishing using hand lines and simple techniques that have been practiced for generations. Join local fishermen for sunset fishing trips and learn about sustainable fishing practices that are central to the Maldivian way of life."]},{"heading":"More Things to Do in Meemu Atoll","paragraphs":["Dive with reef sharks in their natural habitatDuration: 3hrs","Traditional line fishing at sunsetDuration: 2hrs","Experience authentic Maldivian lifeDuration: 4hrs","Private lunch on pristine sandbankDuration: 3hrs","Observe playful dolphins in their natural habitatDuration: 2hrs","Learn to prepare traditional Maldivian dishesDuration: 3hrs"]},{"heading":"Getting to Meemu Atoll","paragraphs":["Meemu Atoll is located approximately 120 km south of Male'' and can be reached by:","For guests staying at Medhufushi Island Resort, the resort arranges combined seaplane transfers from Male'' International Airport. Those staying on local islands can arrange transfers through their guesthouses or use public transportation options."]},{"heading":"Meemu Atoll Transfers","paragraphs":["Male'' to Medhufushi Island Resort","Male'' to Meemu Atoll"]},{"heading":"Best Time to Visit Meemu Atoll","paragraphs":["The best time to visit Meemu Atoll depends on your preferences:","For the ultimate Meemu Atoll experience, visit between December and April when the weather is at its best and underwater visibility is exceptional for diving and snorkeling. This period also coincides with shark season, offering the best chance to encounter these magnificent creatures."]},{"heading":"Discover Meemu Atoll Islands","paragraphs":["Meemu Atoll has a rich cultural heritage that reflects traditional Maldivian island life. The atoll''s relative isolation has helped preserve many traditional practices and customs that have been passed down through generations.","Key cultural highlights include:","Visitors to Meemu Atoll have the unique opportunity to experience authentic Maldivian culture that has been less influenced by tourism than other regions of the country.","The islands of Meemu Atoll maintain strong cultural traditions that are still practiced in daily life. Visitors can witness traditional music and dance performances (Boduberu), observe skilled craftsmen at work, and participate in local festivities during religious and cultural celebrations.","The atoll''s communities are known for their hospitality and willingness to share their cultural heritage with visitors, offering authentic insights into traditional Maldivian island life that has remained largely unchanged for generations."]},{"heading":"Cultural Heritage of Meemu Atoll","paragraphs":["Meemu Atoll has a rich cultural heritage that reflects traditional Maldivian island life. The atoll''s relative isolation has helped preserve many traditional practices and customs that have been passed down through generations.","Key cultural highlights include:","Visitors to Meemu Atoll have the unique opportunity to experience authentic Maldivian culture that has been less influenced by tourism than other regions of the country.","The islands of Meemu Atoll maintain strong cultural traditions that are still practiced in daily life. Visitors can witness traditional music and dance performances (Boduberu), observe skilled craftsmen at work, and participate in local festivities during religious and cultural celebrations.","The atoll''s communities are known for their hospitality and willingness to share their cultural heritage with visitors, offering authentic insights into traditional Maldivian island life that has remained largely unchanged for generations."]}]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'meemu';

-- faafu
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"atoll_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","atoll_sections":[{"heading":"Welcome to Faafu Atoll","paragraphs":["Faafu Atoll (also known as Northern Nilandhe Atoll) is one of the Maldives'' best-kept secrets, offering visitors a glimpse of authentic island life away from the crowds. Located in the central region of the Maldives archipelago, approximately 130 km southwest of Male'', this pristine atoll is characterized by its untouched natural beauty, vibrant coral reefs, and traditional Maldivian communities.","With just a handful of inhabited islands and a few exclusive resorts, Faafu Atoll provides an intimate and authentic Maldivian experience. The atoll''s relative seclusion has preserved its natural environment, making it an ideal destination for travelers seeking tranquility, exceptional diving, and a genuine connection with local culture."]},{"heading":"Best Dive Sites in Faafu Atoll","paragraphs":["One of the Maldives'' most pristine house reefs, featuring vibrant coral gardens, dramatic drop-offs, and an abundance of marine life including reef sharks, eagle rays, and colorful reef fish.","Depth: 5-30m | Level: All levels | Best Time: Year-round","A thrilling drift dive along a dramatic wall featuring overhangs, caves, and a rich variety of marine life including grey reef sharks, Napoleon wrasse, and large schools of snappers and fusiliers.","Depth: 15-40m | Level: Intermediate to Advanced | Best Time: December-April"]},{"heading":"Popular Activities in Faafu Atoll","paragraphs":["Explore the vibrant house reefs surrounding the islands of Faafu Atoll, home to an incredible diversity of marine life and some of the healthiest coral formations in the Maldives.","Visit traditional Maldivian islands like Nilandhoo and Magoodhoo to experience authentic culture, observe local craftsmanship, and learn about the history and heritage of the Maldives.","Experience the time-honored Maldivian tradition of night fishing using hand lines, followed by a beachside BBQ where your fresh catch is prepared by expert local chefs."]},{"heading":"Faafu Atoll Activities","paragraphs":["Explore vibrant coral reefs and marine lifeDuration: 3hrs","Explore local islands & traditional cultureDuration: 6 hrs","Traditional line fishing + BBQ dinnerDuration: 3hrs","Private picnic on pristine sandbankDuration: 4hrs","Romantic sunset cruise with refreshmentsDuration: 2hrs","Explore historical sites & local cultureDuration: 5hrs"]},{"heading":"Getting to Faafu Atoll","paragraphs":["Faafu Atoll is located approximately 130 km southwest of Male'' and can be reached by:","Most visitors to Faafu Atoll stay at one of the luxury resorts, which arrange seaplane transfers directly from Male'' International Airport."]},{"heading":"Best Time to Visit Faafu Atoll","paragraphs":["The best time to visit Faafu Atoll depends on your preferences:","For the ultimate Faafu Atoll experience, visit between December and April when the weather is at its best and underwater visibility is exceptional for diving and snorkeling."]},{"heading":"Discover Faafu Atoll Islands","paragraphs":["Faafu Atoll has a rich cultural heritage that dates back centuries. The atoll''s inhabited islands preserve traditional Maldivian customs, architecture, and way of life that have remained largely unchanged for generations.","Key cultural highlights include:","Visitors to Faafu Atoll have the unique opportunity to experience authentic Maldivian culture that has been preserved due to the atoll''s relative isolation from mass tourism.","The historic mosque in Nilandhoo is one of the oldest Islamic monuments in the Maldives, built during the reign of Sultan Mohamed Bin Abdullah in the 12th century. The mosque features intricate coral stone carvings and traditional Maldivian architectural elements.","Visitors can arrange guided tours to learn about the mosque''s historical significance and the spread of Islam in the Maldives.","Faafu Atoll is truly a hidden gem in the Maldives! We stayed at Filitheyo Island Resort and were blown away by the pristine house reef. Snorkeling right off our water villa, we saw reef sharks, rays, and countless colorful fish. The local island tour to Nilandhoo was also a highlight - such friendly people and fascinating history.","If you''re looking for the authentic Maldives away from the crowds, Faafu Atoll is perfect. We visited during the dry season and had perfect weather. The night fishing experience was unforgettable - we caught our dinner and the resort chef prepared it for us! The only reason for 4 stars instead of 5 is the long transfer time from Male, but it''s worth it for the untouched beauty."]},{"heading":"Cultural Heritage of Faafu Atoll","paragraphs":["Faafu Atoll has a rich cultural heritage that dates back centuries. The atoll''s inhabited islands preserve traditional Maldivian customs, architecture, and way of life that have remained largely unchanged for generations.","Key cultural highlights include:","Visitors to Faafu Atoll have the unique opportunity to experience authentic Maldivian culture that has been preserved due to the atoll''s relative isolation from mass tourism.","The historic mosque in Nilandhoo is one of the oldest Islamic monuments in the Maldives, built during the reign of Sultan Mohamed Bin Abdullah in the 12th century. The mosque features intricate coral stone carvings and traditional Maldivian architectural elements.","Visitors can arrange guided tours to learn about the mosque''s historical significance and the spread of Islam in the Maldives."]}]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'faafu';

-- dhaalu
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"atoll_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","atoll_sections":[{"heading":"Welcome to Dhaalu Atoll","paragraphs":["Dhaalu Atoll, also known as South Nilandhe Atoll, is a beautiful and relatively undeveloped atoll in the central Maldives. Known for its pristine beaches, excellent diving spots, and luxury resorts, Dhaalu Atoll offers visitors a perfect blend of natural beauty and modern comforts.","With its crystal-clear waters, vibrant coral reefs, and laid-back atmosphere, Dhaalu Atoll is an ideal destination for those seeking both relaxation and underwater adventures. The atoll''s capital, Kudahuvadhoo, is home to ancient Buddhist ruins that add a cultural dimension to your visit."]},{"heading":"Best Dive Sites in Dhaalu Atoll","paragraphs":["Spectacular thila (underwater pinnacle) with strong currents attracting large pelagics including sharks, rays, and schools of fish.","Depth: 10-30m | Level: Advanced | Best Time: November-April","Named for its distinctive shape, this site features caves, overhangs, and a rich diversity of marine life including turtles and reef sharks.","Depth: 12-25m | Level: Intermediate | Best Time: Year-round"]},{"heading":"Popular Activities in Dhaalu Atoll","paragraphs":["Explore vibrant coral reefs just steps from your resort with abundant marine life including turtles, rays, and colorful fish.","Visit the capital island to see ancient Buddhist ruins and experience authentic Maldivian culture.","Watch playful dolphins at sunset on a traditional dhoni cruise with refreshments."]},{"heading":"Dhaalu Atoll Activities","paragraphs":["Explore vibrant coral reefs teeming with marine lifeDuration: 2hrs","Discover ancient Buddhist ruins and local cultureDuration: 4 hrs","Watch spinner dolphins at sunsetDuration: 2hrs","Private picnic on pristine sandbankDuration: 4hrs","Deep sea fishing for tuna, wahoo and moreDuration: 5hrs","Explore Dhaalu''s best dive sitesDuration: 3hrs"]},{"heading":"Getting to Dhaalu Atoll","paragraphs":["Dhaalu Atoll is located approximately 150 km southwest of Male'' and can be reached by:","Most luxury resorts in Dhaalu Atoll arrange seaplane transfers directly from Male'' International Airport."]},{"heading":"Best Time to Visit Dhaalu Atoll","paragraphs":["The best time to visit Dhaalu Atoll depends on your interests:","For the best overall experience, visit between December and April when conditions are most favorable for water activities."]},{"heading":"Discover Dhaalu Atoll Islands","paragraphs":["Dhaalu Atoll offers exceptional diving opportunities with healthy coral reefs and abundant marine life. The atoll''s location in the central Maldives means it benefits from nutrient-rich currents that attract large pelagic species.","Common sightings include:","The atoll''s reefs are known for their excellent coral coverage, including both hard and soft corals. Several sites feature dramatic drop-offs, caves, and overhangs that make for exciting dive experiences.","Dhaalu Atoll offers diverse dive sites suitable for all experience levels. Popular sites include Kudarah Thila, Lion''s Head, and several channel dives along the atoll''s edges where you can experience thrilling drift dives.","The atoll''s house reefs are also excellent for snorkeling, with easy access from most resorts and guesthouses."]},{"heading":"Marine Life & Diving","paragraphs":["Dhaalu Atoll offers exceptional diving opportunities with healthy coral reefs and abundant marine life. The atoll''s location in the central Maldives means it benefits from nutrient-rich currents that attract large pelagic species.","Common sightings include:","The atoll''s reefs are known for their excellent coral coverage, including both hard and soft corals. Several sites feature dramatic drop-offs, caves, and overhangs that make for exciting dive experiences.","Dhaalu Atoll offers diverse dive sites suitable for all experience levels. Popular sites include Kudarah Thila, Lion''s Head, and several channel dives along the atoll''s edges where you can experience thrilling drift dives.","The atoll''s house reefs are also excellent for snorkeling, with easy access from most resorts and guesthouses."]}]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'dhaalu';

-- thaa
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"atoll_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","atoll_sections":[{"heading":"Welcome to Thaa Atoll","paragraphs":["Thaa Atoll (also known as Kolhumadulu Atoll) is a beautiful and relatively untouched atoll located in the central Maldives, approximately 240 km southwest of Male''. This horseshoe-shaped atoll consists of 66 islands, with only 13 inhabited by local communities.","Known for its pristine beaches, vibrant coral reefs, and authentic Maldivian culture, Thaa Atoll offers visitors a more secluded and traditional experience compared to the more developed northern atolls. The atoll''s remote location has helped preserve its natural beauty and traditional way of life, making it an ideal destination for travelers seeking tranquility and authenticity."]},{"heading":"Best Dive Sites in Thaa Atoll","paragraphs":["A spectacular dive site featuring a large underwater plateau with coral formations and abundant marine life. Divers can explore the dramatic formations while spotting reef sharks, eagle rays, and schools of tropical fish in crystal-clear waters.","Depth: 12-30m | Level: Intermediate | Best Time: Year-round","A thrilling drift dive along a steep wall with strong currents that attract large pelagic species. Divers regularly encounter grey reef sharks, eagle rays, tuna, and occasionally manta rays and whale sharks.","Depth: 15-40m | Level: Advanced | Best Time: December-April"]},{"heading":"Popular Activities in Thaa Atoll","paragraphs":["Explore some of the Maldives'' most pristine and untouched coral reefs, home to an incredible diversity of marine life including reef sharks, rays, and colorful tropical fish.","Visit traditional Maldivian islands like Veymandoo and Thimarafushi to experience authentic culture, observe local craftsmanship, and interact with friendly locals.","Experience the time-honored Maldivian tradition of night fishing using hand lines, followed by a beachside BBQ where your fresh catch is prepared by expert local chefs."]},{"heading":"Thaa Atoll Activities","paragraphs":["Explore vibrant coral reefs and marine lifeDuration: 3hrs","Explore local islands & traditional cultureDuration: 6 hrs","Traditional line fishing + BBQ dinnerDuration: 3hrs","Private picnic on pristine sandbankDuration: 4hrs","Romantic sunset cruise with refreshmentsDuration: 2hrs","Explore historical sites & local cultureDuration: 5hrs"]},{"heading":"Getting to Thaa Atoll","paragraphs":["Thaa Atoll is located approximately 240 km southwest of Male'' and can be reached by:","Most visitors to Thaa Atoll stay at one of the luxury resorts, which arrange seaplane or domestic flight transfers from Male'' International Airport."]},{"heading":"Thaa Atoll Transfers","paragraphs":["Thaa Atoll"]},{"heading":"Best Time to Visit Thaa Atoll","paragraphs":["The best time to visit Thaa Atoll depends on your preferences:","For the ultimate Thaa Atoll experience, visit between December and April when the weather is at its best and underwater visibility is exceptional for diving and snorkeling."]},{"heading":"Discover Thaa Atoll Islands","paragraphs":["Thaa Atoll has a rich cultural heritage that dates back centuries. The atoll''s inhabited islands preserve traditional Maldivian customs, architecture, and way of life that have remained largely unchanged for generations.","Key cultural highlights include:","Visitors to Thaa Atoll have the unique opportunity to experience authentic Maldivian culture that has been preserved due to the atoll''s relative isolation from mass tourism.","The islands of Thaa Atoll offer visitors a glimpse into traditional Maldivian life. The local communities maintain many ancient customs and traditions, from fishing practices that have sustained island life for centuries to handicrafts that reflect the artistic heritage of the region.","Visitors can arrange cultural tours to learn about the atoll''s history, witness traditional performances, and even participate in craft workshops to learn traditional skills from local artisans."]},{"heading":"Cultural Heritage of Thaa Atoll","paragraphs":["Thaa Atoll has a rich cultural heritage that dates back centuries. The atoll''s inhabited islands preserve traditional Maldivian customs, architecture, and way of life that have remained largely unchanged for generations.","Key cultural highlights include:","Visitors to Thaa Atoll have the unique opportunity to experience authentic Maldivian culture that has been preserved due to the atoll''s relative isolation from mass tourism.","The islands of Thaa Atoll offer visitors a glimpse into traditional Maldivian life. The local communities maintain many ancient customs and traditions, from fishing practices that have sustained island life for centuries to handicrafts that reflect the artistic heritage of the region.","Visitors can arrange cultural tours to learn about the atoll''s history, witness traditional performances, and even participate in craft workshops to learn traditional skills from local artisans."]}]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'thaa';

-- laamu
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"atoll_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","atoll_sections":[{"heading":"Welcome to Laamu Atoll","paragraphs":["Laamu Atoll (also known as Haddhunmathi Atoll) is a pristine paradise located in the central-southern part of the Maldives archipelago, approximately 240 km south of Male''. This stunning atoll offers visitors a perfect blend of luxury, adventure, and authentic Maldivian experiences.","Known for its world-class surfing spots, particularly the famous Yin Yang wave, Laamu Atoll attracts surf enthusiasts from around the globe. Beyond surfing, the atoll boasts pristine beaches, vibrant coral reefs, and a rich marine ecosystem that makes it a haven for divers and snorkelers.","With its mix of luxury resorts, local island experiences, and untouched natural beauty, Laamu Atoll provides an idyllic escape for travelers seeking both relaxation and adventure in one of the Maldives'' most beautiful settings."]},{"heading":"Unique Features of Laamu Atoll","paragraphs":["Laamu Atoll is home to the legendary Yin Yang surf break, one of the most famous waves in the Maldives. This perfect left-hand reef break offers long rides and consistent waves, attracting surfers from around the world during the surf season from April to October.","The atoll features some of the most well-preserved coral reefs in the Maldives, with vibrant marine life and excellent visibility. The Hithadhoo Corner and Maabaidhoo Beyru dive sites are particularly renowned for their healthy coral formations and abundant marine species.","Laamu Atoll is home to unique ecosystems including extensive seagrass meadows and mangrove forests that support a diverse range of marine life. These ecosystems are vital for the atoll''s biodiversity and provide important habitats for endangered species like sea turtles."]},{"heading":"World-Class Surfing in Laamu Atoll","paragraphs":["Laamu Atoll is renowned for its exceptional surfing conditions, particularly at the famous Yin Yang break. The surf season runs from April to October, with the best conditions typically occurring from May to August when consistent swells from the southeast create perfect waves.","The crown jewel of Laamu Atoll''s surf scene, Yin Yang is a world-class left-hand reef break that offers long, powerful rides with multiple sections.","Best Conditions: Southeast swell, northeast winds","Best Season: May to August","Located inside the atoll near Six Senses Laamu, Inside Lefts is a more protected wave that works well when the swell is too big at Yin Yang. This fun left-hander offers more forgiving rides and is suitable for intermediate surfers.","Best Conditions: Southeast swell, any wind direction","Best Season: April to October","A powerful right-hand reef break located on the eastern side of the atoll, Machine offers fast, hollow waves that break over a shallow reef. This wave is best suited for experienced surfers and can produce spectacular barrels in the right conditions.","Best Conditions: Southeast swell, northwest winds","Best Season: May to September","A consistent right-hander located near Maamendhoo Island, Refugees offers fun, rippable walls and occasional barrels. This wave is less crowded than Yin Yang and provides a good alternative for intermediate to advanced surfers.","Best Conditions: Southeast swell, west winds","Best Season: April to October"]},{"heading":"Diving in Laamu Atoll","paragraphs":["A spectacular dive site featuring a dramatic wall drop-off with overhangs and caves. The site is known for its abundant marine life including reef sharks, eagle rays, and large schools of snappers and fusiliers. The healthy hard coral formations make this a photographer''s paradise.","Depth: 10-30m | Level: Intermediate | Best Time: Year-round","A thrilling channel dive known for its strong currents and pelagic encounters. Divers regularly spot grey reef sharks, white-tip sharks, eagle rays, and occasionally manta rays and whale sharks. The channel walls are covered with colorful soft corals and sea fans.","Depth: 15-40m | Level: Advanced | Best Time: December-April"]},{"heading":"Popular Activities in Laamu Atoll","paragraphs":["Explore the vibrant house reefs surrounding the islands of Laamu Atoll, home to an incredible diversity of marine life including reef sharks, rays, turtles, and colorful reef fish. The clear waters and healthy coral formations make for exceptional snorkeling experiences.","Visit multiple islands in Laamu Atoll to experience the diverse landscapes and local culture. From the capital island of Fonadhoo to smaller communities like Maamendhoo and Gan, each island offers unique insights into traditional Maldivian life.","Laamu Atoll is known for its resident spinner dolphin population. Take a boat trip to witness these playful creatures in their natural habitat, often performing acrobatic spins and jumps. Sunset cruises offer particularly magical dolphin encounters."]},{"heading":"More Things to Do in Laamu Atoll","paragraphs":["Ride the legendary left-hand breakDuration: 3hrs","Swim with gentle giants of the oceanDuration: 2 hrs","Traditional line fishing at sunsetDuration: 2hrs","Explore unique marine ecosystemsDuration: 2hrs","Experience authentic Maldivian lifeDuration: 4hrs","Private lunch on pristine sandbankDuration: 3hrs"]},{"heading":"Getting to Laamu Atoll","paragraphs":["Laamu Atoll is located approximately 240 km south of Male'' and can be reached by:","For guests staying at Six Senses Laamu, the resort arranges combined domestic flight and speedboat transfers from Male'' International Airport. Those staying on local islands can arrange transfers through their guesthouses or use public transportation options."]},{"heading":"Laamu Atoll Transfers","paragraphs":["Male'' to Six Senses Laamu","Within Laamu Atoll"]},{"heading":"Best Time to Visit Laamu Atoll","paragraphs":["The best time to visit Laamu Atoll depends on your interests:","For the ultimate Laamu Atoll experience, surfers should visit between May and August, while those interested in diving and snorkeling might prefer December to April when underwater visibility is at its best."]},{"heading":"Discover Laamu Atoll Islands","paragraphs":["Laamu Atoll has a rich cultural heritage that dates back centuries. The atoll''s inhabited islands preserve traditional Maldivian customs, architecture, and way of life that have remained largely unchanged for generations.","Key cultural highlights include:","Visitors to Laamu Atoll have the unique opportunity to experience authentic Maldivian culture by visiting local islands and interacting with communities that maintain their traditional way of life.","One of the most significant archaeological sites in the Maldives, the ancient mound (known locally as \"Havitta\") on Gan Island dates back to the pre-Islamic Buddhist period. The site features the remains of a stupa and other Buddhist structures that provide insights into the Maldives'' pre-Islamic history.","Visitors can arrange cultural tours to learn about the atoll''s history, witness traditional performances, and even participate in craft workshops to learn traditional skills from local artisans.","Laamu Atoll is a surfer''s paradise! I stayed at Six Senses Laamu specifically to surf Yin Yang, and it exceeded all expectations. Perfect left-hander with multiple sections and consistent waves. The resort itself is incredible - sustainable luxury at its finest with amazing food and service. Even if you''re not a surfer, the snorkeling and diving are world-class. Saw manta rays, reef sharks, and countless tropical fish right off the resort''s jetty. Highly recommend!","We spent a week exploring Laamu Atoll, splitting our time between Six Senses and a guesthouse on Gan Island. This gave us a perfect mix of luxury and local experiences. The atoll is less developed than others in the Maldives, which means more authentic culture and pristine nature. The seagrass meadows and marine life are incredible - we saw turtles every day while snorkeling! The only reason for 4 stars instead of 5 is the journey to get there is quite long, but it''s absolutely worth it for the untouched beauty and fewer tourists."]},{"heading":"Cultural Heritage of Laamu Atoll","paragraphs":["Laamu Atoll has a rich cultural heritage that dates back centuries. The atoll''s inhabited islands preserve traditional Maldivian customs, architecture, and way of life that have remained largely unchanged for generations.","Key cultural highlights include:","Visitors to Laamu Atoll have the unique opportunity to experience authentic Maldivian culture by visiting local islands and interacting with communities that maintain their traditional way of life.","One of the most significant archaeological sites in the Maldives, the ancient mound (known locally as \"Havitta\") on Gan Island dates back to the pre-Islamic Buddhist period. The site features the remains of a stupa and other Buddhist structures that provide insights into the Maldives'' pre-Islamic history.","Visitors can arrange cultural tours to learn about the atoll''s history, witness traditional performances, and even participate in craft workshops to learn traditional skills from local artisans."]}]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'laamu';

-- gaafu-alifu
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"atoll_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","atoll_sections":[{"heading":"Welcome to Gaafu Alifu Atoll","paragraphs":["Gaafu Alifu Atoll (also known as North Huvadhoo Atoll) is one of the Maldives'' most pristine and remote destinations, located in the southern reaches of the archipelago. Approximately 400 km south of Male'', this magnificent atoll offers visitors an authentic Maldivian experience far from the more developed tourist areas.","With its spectacular coral reefs, abundant marine life, and traditional island communities, Gaafu Alifu Atoll provides a glimpse into the unspoiled natural beauty and cultural heritage of the Maldives. The atoll''s relative isolation has preserved both its underwater ecosystems and traditional way of life, making it an ideal destination for travelers seeking authenticity and tranquility."]},{"heading":"Best Dive Sites in Gaafu Alifu Atoll","paragraphs":["A spectacular dive site featuring a large underwater cavern with multiple entrances. Divers can explore the dramatic formations while spotting reef sharks, eagle rays, and schools of tropical fish in crystal-clear waters.","Depth: 10-30m | Level: Intermediate to Advanced | Best Time: Year-round","A thrilling drift dive along a steep wall with strong currents that attract large pelagic species. Divers regularly encounter grey reef sharks, eagle rays, tuna, and occasionally manta rays and whale sharks.","Depth: 15-40m | Level: Advanced | Best Time: December-April"]},{"heading":"Popular Activities in Gaafu Alifu Atoll","paragraphs":["Explore some of the Maldives'' most pristine and untouched coral reefs, home to an incredible diversity of marine life including reef sharks, rays, and colorful tropical fish.","Visit traditional Maldivian islands like Vilingili, Dhaandhoo, and Kolamaafushi to experience authentic culture, observe local craftsmanship, and interact with friendly locals.","Experience the time-honored Maldivian tradition of night fishing using hand lines, followed by a beachside BBQ where your fresh catch is prepared by expert local chefs."]},{"heading":"Gaafu Alifu Atoll Activities","paragraphs":["Explore vibrant coral reefs and marine lifeDuration: 3hrs","Explore local islands & traditional cultureDuration: 6 hrs","Traditional line fishing + BBQ dinnerDuration: 3hrs","Private picnic on pristine sandbankDuration: 4hrs","Romantic sunset cruise with refreshmentsDuration: 2hrs","Explore historical sites & local cultureDuration: 5hrs"]},{"heading":"Getting to Gaafu Alifu Atoll","paragraphs":["Gaafu Alifu Atoll is located approximately 400 km south of Male'' and can be reached by:","Most visitors to Gaafu Alifu Atoll stay at one of the luxury resorts, which arrange domestic flight and speedboat transfers from Male'' International Airport."]},{"heading":"Gaafu Alifu Atoll Transfers","paragraphs":["Gaafu Alifu Atoll","Gaafu Alifu Atoll","Gaafu Alifu Atoll"]},{"heading":"Best Time to Visit Gaafu Alifu Atoll","paragraphs":["The best time to visit Gaafu Alifu Atoll depends on your preferences:","For the ultimate Gaafu Alifu Atoll experience, visit between December and April when the weather is at its best and underwater visibility is exceptional for diving and snorkeling."]},{"heading":"Discover Gaafu Alifu Atoll Islands","paragraphs":["Gaafu Alifu Atoll has a rich cultural heritage that dates back centuries. The atoll''s inhabited islands preserve traditional Maldivian customs, architecture, and way of life that have remained largely unchanged for generations due to the atoll''s remote location.","Key cultural highlights include:","Visitors to Gaafu Alifu Atoll have the unique opportunity to experience authentic Maldivian culture that has been preserved due to the atoll''s relative isolation from mass tourism.","The islands of Gaafu Alifu Atoll offer visitors a glimpse into traditional Maldivian life. The local communities maintain many ancient customs and traditions, from fishing practices that have sustained island life for centuries to handicrafts that reflect the artistic heritage of the region.","Visitors can arrange cultural tours to learn about the atoll''s history, witness traditional performances, and even participate in craft workshops to learn traditional skills from local artisans."]},{"heading":"Cultural Heritage of Gaafu Alifu Atoll","paragraphs":["Gaafu Alifu Atoll has a rich cultural heritage that dates back centuries. The atoll''s inhabited islands preserve traditional Maldivian customs, architecture, and way of life that have remained largely unchanged for generations due to the atoll''s remote location.","Key cultural highlights include:","Visitors to Gaafu Alifu Atoll have the unique opportunity to experience authentic Maldivian culture that has been preserved due to the atoll''s relative isolation from mass tourism.","The islands of Gaafu Alifu Atoll offer visitors a glimpse into traditional Maldivian life. The local communities maintain many ancient customs and traditions, from fishing practices that have sustained island life for centuries to handicrafts that reflect the artistic heritage of the region.","Visitors can arrange cultural tours to learn about the atoll''s history, witness traditional performances, and even participate in craft workshops to learn traditional skills from local artisans."]}]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'gaafu-alifu';

-- gaafu-dhaalu
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"atoll_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","atoll_sections":[{"heading":"Welcome to Gaafu Dhaalu Atoll","paragraphs":["Gaafu Dhaalu Atoll (also known as South Huvadhoo Atoll) is a pristine and remote destination in the southern Maldives, located just south of Gaafu Alifu Atoll. Approximately 450 km south of Male'', this magnificent atoll offers visitors an authentic Maldivian experience with its untouched natural beauty and rich cultural heritage.","With its spectacular coral reefs, abundant marine life, and traditional island communities, Gaafu Dhaalu Atoll provides a glimpse into the unspoiled natural beauty of the Maldives. The atoll''s relative isolation has preserved both its underwater ecosystems and traditional way of life, making it an ideal destination for travelers seeking authenticity and tranquility."]},{"heading":"Best Dive Sites in Gaafu Dhaalu Atoll","paragraphs":["A thrilling channel dive with strong currents that attract large pelagic species. Divers regularly encounter grey reef sharks, eagle rays, tuna, and occasionally manta rays and whale sharks.","Depth: 15-40m | Level: Advanced | Best Time: December-April","A spectacular dive site featuring dramatic coral formations and abundant marine life. Divers can explore the reef while spotting reef sharks, eagle rays, and schools of tropical fish in crystal-clear waters.","Depth: 10-30m | Level: Intermediate to Advanced | Best Time: Year-round"]},{"heading":"Popular Activities in Gaafu Dhaalu Atoll","paragraphs":["Explore some of the Maldives'' most pristine and untouched coral reefs, home to an incredible diversity of marine life including reef sharks, rays, and colorful tropical fish.","Visit traditional Maldivian islands like Thinadhoo, Gadhdhoo, and Vaadhoo to experience authentic culture, observe local craftsmanship, and interact with friendly locals.","Experience the time-honored Maldivian tradition of night fishing using hand lines, followed by a beachside BBQ where your fresh catch is prepared by expert local chefs."]},{"heading":"Gaafu Dhaalu Atoll Activities","paragraphs":["Explore vibrant coral reefs and marine lifeDuration: 3hrs","Explore local islands & traditional cultureDuration: 6 hrs","Traditional line fishing + BBQ dinnerDuration: 3hrs","Private picnic on pristine sandbankDuration: 4hrs","Romantic sunset cruise with refreshmentsDuration: 2hrs","Explore historical sites & local cultureDuration: 5hrs"]},{"heading":"Getting to Gaafu Dhaalu Atoll","paragraphs":["Gaafu Dhaalu Atoll is located approximately 450 km south of Male'' and can be reached by:","Most visitors to Gaafu Dhaalu Atoll stay at one of the luxury resorts, which arrange domestic flight and speedboat transfers from Male'' International Airport."]},{"heading":"Gaafu Dhaalu Atoll Transfers","paragraphs":["Gaafu Dhaalu Atoll","Gaafu Dhaalu Atoll"]},{"heading":"Best Time to Visit Gaafu Dhaalu Atoll","paragraphs":["The best time to visit Gaafu Dhaalu Atoll depends on your preferences:","For the ultimate Gaafu Dhaalu Atoll experience, visit between December and April when the weather is at its best and underwater visibility is exceptional for diving and snorkeling."]},{"heading":"Discover Gaafu Dhaalu Atoll Islands","paragraphs":["Gaafu Dhaalu Atoll has a rich cultural heritage that dates back centuries. The atoll''s inhabited islands preserve traditional Maldivian customs, architecture, and way of life that have remained largely unchanged for generations due to the atoll''s remote location.","Key cultural highlights include:","Visitors to Gaafu Dhaalu Atoll have the unique opportunity to experience authentic Maldivian culture that has been preserved due to the atoll''s relative isolation from mass tourism.","The islands of Gaafu Dhaalu Atoll offer visitors a glimpse into traditional Maldivian life. The local communities maintain many ancient customs and traditions, from fishing practices that have sustained island life for centuries to handicrafts that reflect the artistic heritage of the region.","Visitors can arrange cultural tours to learn about the atoll''s history, witness traditional performances, and even participate in craft workshops to learn traditional skills from local artisans."]},{"heading":"Cultural Heritage of Gaafu Dhaalu Atoll","paragraphs":["Gaafu Dhaalu Atoll has a rich cultural heritage that dates back centuries. The atoll''s inhabited islands preserve traditional Maldivian customs, architecture, and way of life that have remained largely unchanged for generations due to the atoll''s remote location.","Key cultural highlights include:","Visitors to Gaafu Dhaalu Atoll have the unique opportunity to experience authentic Maldivian culture that has been preserved due to the atoll''s relative isolation from mass tourism.","The islands of Gaafu Dhaalu Atoll offer visitors a glimpse into traditional Maldivian life. The local communities maintain many ancient customs and traditions, from fishing practices that have sustained island life for centuries to handicrafts that reflect the artistic heritage of the region.","Visitors can arrange cultural tours to learn about the atoll''s history, witness traditional performances, and even participate in craft workshops to learn traditional skills from local artisans."]}]}'::jsonb
